    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Consumptive water use or evapotranspiration (ET) for crops and riparian vegetation is required in the hydrologic budget of a region for water management purposes. The demand for managing water in near real-time is increasing due to scarcity of water especially in arid environments. Due to this near real-time demand, water managers and decision makers are increasingly interested in the computer based hydrologic models to provide estimates of water budget of a region. Current hydrologic models use either direct measured values or indirect calculated values that depend on meteorological data as input to the model.\r\n\r\nA methodology for estimating ET of saltcedar (Tamarix spp.) using a polynomial crop coefficient as a function of heat units is presented. This methodology could easily be implemented as an improvement in estimating ET of saltcedar in existing hydrologic models.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
